  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41123" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connecting sectoral ministries, markets, and entrepreneurs to financing mechanisms to improve smallholder livelihoods and income</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Joint Programme (JP) aims to catalyse a systemic transformation of Cameroon#s agribusiness sector through an integrated grow#tra nsform#connect#finance#sustain model aligned with climate and nature priorities. Addressing fragmented governance, limited technical capacity and finance, and persistent gender inequalities, the JP leverages the comparative advantages of WFP, UNIDO, FAO, UNEP and UNCDF under the leadership of the Resident Coordinator.  Expected results include strengthened whole-of-government, multi-sectoral governance; empowered Ecosystems of Support (EoS); improved processing and food safety infrastructure; increased adoption of climate-smart and agroecological practices; and expanded income and employment opportunities for women and youth across four value chains (rice, cassava, eggs and milk).  Phase I (one year) will pilot interventions in the Far North, East and Adamawa regions with 44 cooperatives and MSMEs, focusing on EoS strengthening, financial literacy, and the screening of financial service providers and eligible enterprises. Phase II (two years) will scale up support to 380 cooperatives/MSMEs.</narrative>
  </description>
